WEBVTT

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:08.650
What's the big idea?!

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:11.320
You traitor.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.690
Are you in any position to call me that?

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:18.790
How was what I did any different from what you're trying to do now?

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:33.710
I would never sell out a friend.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:00.660
I feel like it'll disappear...

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:06.390
...the instant I look away.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:11.530
I just kept counting...

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:16.970
...all the many traces of loneliness...

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:24.340
...that I'd vomited up.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:30.280
In this time that seems so dry,

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:35.390
...my heart is thrashing around and drowning.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:41.250
It takes those lies that make my head spin...

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:44.300
...and tears them to pieces.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:53.970
 And the place I lose my way in...

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:01.800
...is a dim, hazy world.

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:23.250
So, find anything?

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.310
It's me. You there?

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:41.430
Hm? Yes.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:43.140
Can I come in?

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:47.200
Sorry. It's okay. The door's unlocked.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:53.080
I found a guy who says he saw somebody resembling Amon.

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:54.670
He saw Amon?

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:57.840
Yeah, and twice in the same place, to boot.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:02.430
He was scoping out a house all day from a car parked on the side of the road.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:03.830
Why would he do that?

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:08.320
Beats me, but if we go to that house, we might find out something.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:11.100
What do you say? Wanna go check it out with me?

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:15.670
National Public
Safety Commission

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:15.670
National
 Police Agency

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:25.820
I'm terribly sorry, the Commissioner is in a meeting at the moment,

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:28.020
...so please wait here for a few minutes.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.950
Hm? Y- Yes, of course.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.420
Damn, we're back to square one.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.560
No luck?

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:44.860
Yeah. An old lady's been living in that house by herself for a long time.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:49.830
Amon tailed somebody here. No doubt about it.

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:51.570
That's what I think, anyway.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:56.810
Maybe Amon came here to ask her about someone else.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.350
The only thing that old lady can tell us about is ancient history.

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:02.910
Who could he possibly ask her about?!

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:13.730
Overconfidence...

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:14.570
Huh?

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:18.500
Me, I mean. Everything's come easy so far,

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:21.870
...so maybe I've been jumping to conclusions and simplifying Amon's motives.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:25.570
Where are we going?

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:27.650
Preliminary digging.

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:31.710
If he asked the old lady something, we need to clear the decks first.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:33.320
Clear the decks?

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:36.120
Yeah. We're gonna go find out...

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:39.850
...if anybody connected to the old lady might attract Amon's attention.

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:50.730
I called you here today for a reason.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:52.140
Yes, sir...

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:53.370
You drink tea, don't you?

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:56.440
Hm? Y- Yes, of course. Tea is fine, sir.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:00.470
I'm sorry, but could you bring some hot tea for myself and Inspector Kosaka?

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:02.140
Right away, sir.

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:05.640
It will be here in a minute.

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:08.650
Yes, sir. Thank you, sir.

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:14.790
Anyway, to get back to why I had you come all the way down here,

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:21.400
...your reports suggest that Administrator Zaizen hasn't been seen at your office for some time.

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:23.100
Yes, sir.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:26.670
It would seem that various matters have kept the Administrator busy...

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:29.470
...since the attack on the STN-J.

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:31.540
There has been no word from him?

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:33.850
Not for the past month or so.

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:35.910
I see...

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:39.020
Um, is the Administrator in some sort of trouble?

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:40.220
Yes...

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:46.850
There seems to be some trouble between Mr. Zaizen and Solomon headquarters.

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:50.030
It is still just a possibility at this point,

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:56.130
...but Zaizen's standing within Solomon Japan may undergo some changes in the near future.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:02.040
Naturally, we have no intention of making an enemy of him just yet.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:08.340
For the time being, we will need to keep a close eye on their power plays.

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:15.210
And that brings me a small matter which will require your cooperation.

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:34.700
A 40% cut in the project budget?! What's going on here?

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:37.780
Yes, sir?

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:40.770
Get me the chief accountant of Solomon's Japan branch...

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:44.640
No, wait. Get me CFO Sugimura.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:49.420
CFO Sugimura of the Japan branch, sir? One moment, please.

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:57.590
Administrator, Mr. Sugimura isn't answering my call.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.190
What's going on?

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:00.660
I'm not sure, sir.

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:06.090
Just in case, I tried calling other departments, but there is no answer at any of them.

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:07.170
Oh, I see...

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:11.540
I hate to trouble you, but wait a while and then try reaching them again.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:13.100
Understood.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:19.510
Pressure from headquarters? Or could it be...

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:25.960
A hunter from headquarters?

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:29.490
They went over my head? But why?

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:36.790
Oh. They're planning to oust me, are they?

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:39.760
It's me.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:43.130
I'd like you to get verification on something for me.

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:45.640
No, it's not that.

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:48.610
It's about Solomon Japan's Finance & Administration Department.

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:56.320
Looks like we're in for a little rain...

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:59.290
Hall of Records

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:59.290
Browsing Room

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:10.200
Find out anything?

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:15.660
Yeah. The old lady's only son lived there for a while.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:18.130
So you think Amon was looking for that man?

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:22.610
What's the matter?

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:25.580
Hm? He lived there, all right, but...

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:29.110
Well, the guy died 15 years ago.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:34.560
What would make Amon chase after ancient history like that?

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:38.230
So it wasn't him, then.

00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:39.530
Maybe, maybe not.

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:41.320
Where to now?

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.790
The university he worked at.

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:56.970
Mornin', all.

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:58.580
Good morning.

00:08:58.920 --> 00:08:59.710
Hi.

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:01.450
Does it look like morning out there to you?

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:10.220
And a fine morning to you, Chief.

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:11.990
Yeah, good morning.

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:18.390
Has the Chief lost it?

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:20.840
Why ask me? How should I know?

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:34.620
Ah, here it is.

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:38.750
Hiroshi Toudou. This is him, right?

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:13.490
Really?

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:17.730
I'm starting to get the big picture.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:22.290
Looks like the reason the dead son left his assistant professor position here...

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:25.460
...was because he was scouted by a European corporation.

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:26.900
European?

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:29.700
Yeah, FZ Genemics.

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:34.070
It's a pharmaceutical company that was once rumored to have ties to Solomon.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:35.780
Solomon...!

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:39.250
Looks like the pieces are starting to fall into place, huh?

00:10:43.020 --> 00:10:46.180
The hunter's name is Willem Hasselbaink. Age, 42.

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:48.220
He's a hunter from Holland.

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:51.290
What about this hunter's movements?

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:53.860
We've determined his route of entry into the country.

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:58.540
We should be able to determine his movements inside the country any time now.

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:01.410
Put more people on it if you have to.

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:02.960
Put a rush on this investigation.

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:06.910
Memories of death...

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:11.810
So, this is where you... Corneli...

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:18.460
Yes?

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:20.480
I'm terribly sorry to disturb you at this hour.

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:26.160
My name is Takane. I worked as a research assistant at Professor Toudou's lab.

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:30.800
The thing is, the lab is putting together an alumni registry, so l...

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:33.530
You must be Mr. Nagira.

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:35.700
Uh... Yes, ma'am.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:38.510
I was told to expect you.

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:48.380
Is something the matter, ma'am?

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:52.520
Um, no, not at all. Please, come in.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:57.680
How did she know?

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:01.160
Who else? It must have been Amon.

00:12:03.170 --> 00:12:05.640
So, it WAS giving us an invitation.

00:12:10.070 --> 00:12:12.600
Everything is exactly as it was 15 years ago.

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:19.580
I haven't touched anything in here since it happened.

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:23.290
Since... what happened, ma'am?

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:28.450
It's nothing. I'm sorry, you'll have to excuse me.

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:33.590
If you want to take a closer look at anything, feel free to move things around.

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:39.630
Dig around all we want, huh?

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:41.910
She sure seems to know everything...

00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:47.800
Well, shall we avail ourselves of her hospitality and dig around to our hearts' content, then?

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:08.030
I don't understand any of this.

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:12.870
That's no surprise. But Amon was definitely checking up on something here.

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:15.770
We ought to be able to figure out what that was.

00:13:27.150 --> 00:13:28.280
A diary?

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:40.360
Hey, the stuff in this is from when Toudou worked at that European research agency.

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:43.860
What's the matter?

00:13:48.670 --> 00:13:50.440
A picture of Toudou, huh?

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:55.800
Hey, she's a real hottie...

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:57.610
She kinda looks like you.

00:13:57.950 --> 00:13:59.780
Nah, maybe not...

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:05.480
Come to think of it, the old lady looked a little shocked when she saw you.

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:09.520
Maybe she thought you looked like this woman.

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:11.160
Nagira, let's go.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:13.060
Huh? Why the big rush?

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:16.030
Hey, wait up!

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:25.740
Hey, Robin!

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:31.740
I'm sorry, do you mind if I borrowed this?

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:33.270
Go right ahead.

00:14:35.590 --> 00:14:38.210
Thanks for the tea. If you'll excuse us...

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:55.640
Huh? I thought you were heading home for the night, Lady Dojima.

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:57.940
I forgot something, that's all.

00:14:57.940 --> 00:15:00.710
Plus, I thought I'd bring a treat for the prisoner.

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:02.770
Hey, thanks as always.

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:04.580
You're quite welcome.

00:15:08.850 --> 00:15:11.420
Oh, right. Michael, have you ever heard of something...

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:13.290
...called the Solomon Genetic Research Team?

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:17.490
Genetic Research Team?
No, sorry. What brought this on?

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:21.500
I only heard the name, myself, so I don't know what it is.

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:23.030
But it sure sounds interesting, doesn't it?

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:25.070
What's your source?

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:27.970
That's a secret. Anyway, I'm outta here.

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:32.870
The Genetic Research Team...

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:47.290
We have confirmation on the hunter.

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:49.090
The same as this afternoon?

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:50.750
Yes, sir. The exact same location.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:53.030
Is he waiting for something?

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:53.730
Sir?

00:15:53.730 --> 00:15:57.860
Never mind. So, the hunter is just standing there, then?

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:10.070
It's freezing...

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:15.080
She's still far away...

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:18.340
Op concluded. Returning to base.

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:24.050
Oh, crap!

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:27.120
Get the doctor! Something's wrong with zero-two!

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:52.670
Get me the security division at HQ! Now!

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:59.650
I see. Yes, forward the assault data to the foundation.

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:04.260
Make no mention whatsoever of Orbo's side effects.

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:06.060
Is that clear?

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:15.200
Well, now... This has now become an all-out war with headquarters.

00:18:23.050 --> 00:18:24.450
A Factory van?

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:36.420
Those are...

00:18:46.070 --> 00:18:48.300
I wonder if this is a code word for something.

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:51.140
There's a symbol that keeps popping up.

00:18:51.910 --> 00:18:54.670
Is that an omega? No, maybe it's pi.

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:58.250
Something about "Analysis of the pi genome is almost complete."

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:00.550
"Pi then becomes a genetic factor."

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:04.750
"With this, a means of controlling the abilities has been opened to us."

00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:06.660
What does that mean?

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:11.190
This "pi" thing was probably the focus of the research he was involved in.

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:15.890
Whatever it is, it's definitely got something to do with genetic engineering.

00:19:16.430 --> 00:19:18.300
Amon was chasing after it.

00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:21.400
Which would mean that it's about the link between genetics and Witches?

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:27.410
No, this bit here about controlling abilities... That's not enough to...

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:28.340
Orbo!

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:30.870
Or-what? What's that?

00:19:31.220 --> 00:19:32.740
Nothing, forget it.

00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:39.210
Anyway, Nagira, is there anything in the diary about a priest named Juliano?

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:40.820
Juliano?

00:19:42.690 --> 00:19:43.690
Doesn't look like it.

00:19:43.690 --> 00:19:44.600
Oh.

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:47.330
Who's this Juliano guy?

00:19:47.570 --> 00:19:49.360
Nobody. Forget it.

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:54.790
At any rate, it looks like we're gonna have to look a little deeper into this thing.

00:19:55.370 --> 00:19:57.740
Still, I guess it's too late to do anything about it today.

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:03.000
For the time being, I'm gonna break up this little meeting.

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:07.750
You should call it a day and get some sleep, too.

00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:09.380
I know.

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:37.310
Why...?

00:20:39.850 --> 00:20:41.750
What was he doing there?

00:20:46.190 --> 00:20:47.590
Why...?

00:20:49.090 --> 00:20:50.080
Juliano...

00:20:59.470 --> 00:21:01.130
Damn it, it's really starting to...

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:06.170
I knew it.

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:11.000
You deliberately left a trail so that I'd be able to follow you, didn't you?

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:15.220
What are you up to?

00:21:15.220 --> 00:21:17.310
I'm going to hunt Robin.

00:21:17.660 --> 00:21:19.450
Wha...? What did you just say?

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:21.560
I'm going to hunt Robin.

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:25.890
Are you out of your mind?

00:21:26.460 --> 00:21:27.930
I'm not crazy.

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:31.200
But Robin has become the most dangerous Witch of all.

00:21:31.740 --> 00:21:33.860
What're you talking about? A Witch, huh?

00:21:34.470 --> 00:21:36.960
That's just the way that Solomon's decided to see her.

00:21:39.510 --> 00:21:43.110
This isn't because of some unresolved issues with your mother, is it?

00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:45.480
It's not.

00:21:45.480 --> 00:21:47.040
Then what the hell are you saying?!

00:21:48.190 --> 00:21:50.420
You must have seen it. You must have seen Robin's power.

00:21:50.820 --> 00:21:52.950
That doesn't matter to me.

00:21:53.190 --> 00:21:54.590
Robin is Robin.

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:57.890
She hasn't changed one bit since the day you left her with me.

00:21:59.560 --> 00:22:03.520
Listen, it's not a person's past that tells you whether or not to trust them.

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:06.870
It's whether you can trust that person's heart right now.

00:22:07.400 --> 00:22:14.070
At the very least, you must've believed in her back when you entrusted her to me.

00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:16.840
Are you trying to tell me that was a mistake?

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:22.440
I'm gonna protect Robin, even if it means taking a bullet for...

00:22:24.660 --> 00:22:25.750
Amon...

00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:44.990
Just how far back do I need to go?

00:22:44.810 --> 00:22:47.850
Tell me.

00:22:49.060 --> 00:22:59.840
It's all so vivid that it hurts.

00:23:00.700 --> 00:23:09.730
The truth is, nothing can be shared,

00:23:09.410 --> 00:23:14.220
...so I never looked back.

00:23:15.490 --> 00:23:19.590
...all those promises...

00:23:21.530 --> 00:23:25.990
...inside me eventually...

00:23:25.280 --> 00:23:31.790
...gave up on that light from some other time,

00:23:30.990 --> 00:23:40.570
...like the light of a morning you can't return to.
